Hi Angelo

Angelo Machils wrote:
 > best use a RW disk..... But now the next problem, the install doesn't
 > 'see' any harddrives..... :(

As of your SRM device listing you seem to have a QLogic ISP controller. 
This should be in the default kernel according to the installation 
manual (section 2.2.1). You may have greater success with an official CD 
image or you can try to preload the required module (qlogicisp; see 
chapter 10.4 of the i386 manual). If you do not want to download a whole 
cd-image you may install from floppy disks: You just need the rescue and 
root floppy.

Regards, Adrian.



