Me again.  I can't let go of those old Alpha 4100s.  They are like an
old car on blocks in the yard that I tinker with now again hoping to
turn the engine over.  One day they will move our Windows file systems
off the MSA1000 and if I have't made Debian boot on the Alphas by then,
I will just call a tow truck and have them hauled away.  But in the
meantime, with much help from Steve and others on this list, we am
inching forward.  Sarge RC1 sees the DAC960 and the volumes on it; I can
=66ormat them; I understand to leave an aboot partition (and it even
prompts me if I forget) but it still fails at kernel install time with:

Setting up kernel-image-2.4.26-1-generic (--configure):
depmod: *** Unresolved symbols in
/lib/modules/2.4.26-1-generic/kernel/drivers/char/scx200.o
/usr/sbin/mkinitrd: device /dev/rd/c0d0p1 is not a block device
=46ailed to create initrd image.
dpkg: error processing kernel-image-2.4.26-1-generic (--configure):
  subprocess post-installation-script returned error exit status 2
Errors were encountered while processing:
  kernel-image-2.4.26-1-generic
E: Sub-process /usr/bin/dpkg returned an error code (1)

I think this is the problem Steve mentioned that has been isolated and
should be fixed in RC1; I am still seeing it.  Will try the daily build
and a Sid and see what happens.  This is more an FYI than a "help!"

John

