Joakim Roubert <jokke@df.lth.se> writes:
> I made some experiments with 2.6.3, but never got around to finish the
> job. Now I am trying to migrate to 2.6.8. I had the 2.6.3 to run, but can
> not make my 2.6.8 boot correctly; it seems the SCSI settings are not
> correct. Of course I have not kept my 2.6.3 settings. :(
> 
> Machine is an AlphaStation 200 4/166, and I use the standard on board
> NCR53c810 SCSI card. I currently run 2.4.20 with no problems.

A while ago I posted here and got the following response:

> Okay, I've now tested stock 2.6.7 without debian patches and the
> situation is the same: the sym53c8xx_2 driver doesn't work but fails on
> boot with messages about timeouts and resets.
> 
> Has anyone had better experience with 2.6.x kernels on AS200?

I had this problem on a LX164 machine.  The problem seemed to be a missing 
CONFIG_ define which used to be in old versions of the kernel, but has 
disappeared in recent versions.  Unfortunately, quite a lot of the alpha code 
still expects it.

If I remember correctly, it was CONFIG_ALPHA_SRM.

My .config is attached, in case it helps.  This is from the 2.6.6 kernel that 
I'm running on this machine.  You will need to change it, I suppose, as far as 
the actual machine type is concerned.

